        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0988" n="976" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg976"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Press Release Issued at Nanking on June 5</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Nanking</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1946-06-05">June 5, 1946</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>The Committee of Three has directed the movement of an advance Section of
                    Executive Headquarters to Changchun, there to get established <pb facs="0989"
                        n="977" xml:id="pg977"/> in preparation for carrying out whatever agreements
                    may be reached for the cessation of hostilities. Brigadier General Henry A.
                    Byroade will be the senior American Officer in this Advance Section. Brigadier
                    General Thomas S. Timberman will temporarily take over General Byroade’s duties
                    in Peiping.</p>
            </div>
